<h2>Appeal Process</h2>
<p>If you disagree with an assessment decision, you have the right to appeal.</p>
<ol>
<li>When the assessor gives you feedback, say whether you agree with the outcome. If you agree, you and the assessor sign the Assessment Summary Record; if you disagree, do not sign it.</li>
<li>Discuss the decision with the assessor or the assessment manager first.</li>
<li>If you are still not satisfied, tell the assessor you intend to appeal. The assessor records this in the feedback section of the Assessment Summary Record and informs the assessment manager.</li>
<li>Lodge your appeal within <strong>7 days</strong>, giving your reasons, using the <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/u/1/d/e/1FAIpQLSf8CcVv_ITUOWE75kV6H7dCaJ5-skqcdfpqSV-Bmn8Pjdx4pg/viewform?usp=send_form"<?php echo $_ext; ?>>Candidate Appeal Form</a>. The assessor can help you write and lodge it.</li>
<li>An Assessment Appeal Panel reviews the information from you and the assessor and makes a decision. A record of the appeal and its outcome is kept.</li>
<li>You will be told the outcome within <strong>2 weeks</strong> of lodging the appeal. The panel's decision is final.</li>
</ol>
